+## 2026-10-09 — DFlash2 is not dead: fp16 overflow + freed-KV reads past the window (both fixed)
+
+**VERDICT:** `SHIPPED` · **GATE:** serving A/B on fork `main` (`6ccbb03`), 2× MI50 16 GB
+(TP=2, both cards capped at 90 W), Qwen3.8-27B-AWQ-INT4 + `z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2`
+(byte-identical to `incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2`, sha256 `67fc76d6…`), k=7, V2, float16,
+max-len 32768, max-num-seqs 1, bt 1024, capture `[8]`, prefix caching off, KV pinned 2 GiB.
+"bench" = 6 chat-templated 512-token greedy generations (prose / code / reasoning × 2);
+the long rows are one code-reading prompt each (tg 384, greedy).
+
+### HYPOTHESIS
+
+If the 0 % acceptance of 2026-09-15/16 comes from our numerics/plumbing rather than the
+checkpoint, then keeping the draft's residual stream inside fp16 range and keeping its sliding
+window in the non-causal FA path restore the model card's acceptance (4–5 tokens/step).
+
+### What was done
+
+- **Root cause 1 — fp16 overflow (every context).** vllm#55250: the bf16-trained draft's
+  residual stream passes 65504 by its second layer, goes inf/NaN, the candidates degrade to ids
+  0..top_k-1 and acceptance is exactly 0. Every arm in this log, the bf16-pair run and the
+  5070 Ti run in `HANDOVER-dflash2.md` ran the draft in fp16 (gfx906 has no bf16; fp16 targets
+  cast the draft). Fix: `rescale_residual_stream` (`qwen3_dflash2.py`) scales o_proj, the up
+  half of gate_up_proj and down_proj (and the layer-0 residual) by a power of two at load time.
+  Every branch reads the stream through an RMSNorm and the grouped conv's `finish` is linear in
+  the branch output, so nothing the draft computes changes. fp16 drafts only;
+  `VLLM_DFLASH2_FP16_RESIDUAL_DIVISOR=1` turns it off.
+- **Root cause 2 — window dropped (context > ~2k).** FA-NONCAUSAL stage 1 zeroes `window` for
+  non-causal batches, so the draft attended over `[0, seq_len)`; the KV manager frees a sliding
+  layer's blocks once they leave the window, so past ~2–4k the draft read freed blocks and
+  acceptance fell to exactly 0 again. Fix (`gfx906_fa_paged.py`, Python only):
+  `q_abs_offset = seq_len` and `window + n_q` express "no causal clip, left window only" with
+  the existing mask, and the gather clip is kept (`DEVLOG-fa-noncausal.md` 2026-10-09).
+- Tests: `test_dflash2_residual_rescale_is_exact`, `test_dflash2_residual_rescale_keeps_fp16_finite`
+  (`tests/v1/spec_decode/test_dflash2.py`), `test_non_causal_sliding_window_never_reads_freed_blocks[64|200]`
+  (`tests/kernels/attention/test_gfx906_fa.py`; fails on the previous code). `test_gfx906_fa.py` +
+  `test_dflash2.py` + `test_dflash_causality.py`: **127 passed**.
+
+### Evidence — FOR (gate above; t/s with tokens/step in parentheses)
+
+| arm | bench | 1.5k | 4.6k | 14.6k | 24.4k |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `main` | 10.21 (1.01) | 9.65 (1.00) | — | — | — |
+| + fp16 rescale only | 48.42 (4.82) | 39.47 (4.03) | 9.61 (1.00) | 8.76 (1.00) | — |
+| + rescale + window | **46.54 (4.65)** | **39.63 (4.03)** | **34.84 (3.66)** | **32.75 (3.70)** | **31.40 (3.85)** |
+
+Per-position acceptance (server log, 10-s windows, both fixes): pos 0 between 0.54 (prose) and
+0.94 (code/reasoning); a code window reads 0.94 / 0.83 / 0.71 / 0.63 / 0.53 / 0.45 / 0.40. The
+2026-09-15 runs read 0.04 / 0.06 / 0.0 at pos 0.
+
+### Evidence — AGAINST / limits
+
+- Not yet gated against MTP k=3 on the 32 GB production config (agentic corpus, 64k/120k). On
+  this 16 GB / 90 W box, bench MTP k=3 (V1, max-len 32768, 4 seqs) read 49.9 t/s, a tie on
+  average: DFlash2 wins on code and reasoning, loses on prose.
+- The 3.6 GB draft costs ~1.8 GiB/rank. On 16 GB cards that limits DFlash2 to ~32k context and
+  1 sequence.
+- Prefix caching stays off for DFlash2 on hybrid targets (vLLM#48375 unmerged).
+
+### Why the 2026-09-16 verdict was wrong
+
+Each suspect was "excluded" by a run whose draft was fp16, so root cause 1 masked every
+experiment. The bf16-pair run used `--dtype float16` too, which this fork requires. PR #38
+(v0.28.0 line, open) found the same overflow independently and fixes it with an fp32 residual
+stream. #41 ported #38's small fixes to the 0.30.0 line without this one.
+
